WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.450
This is Allen Company training on surface operations

00:07.450 --> 00:10.825
hazards: water, spoil banks and stockpiles,

00:10.825 --> 00:13.537
the pit itself, and working in low light.

00:13.537 --> 00:16.238
Clover Bottom has a surface pit, and every site

00:16.238 --> 00:19.625
has surface stockpiles, ponds and haul roads.

00:19.625 --> 00:22.363
Highwalls and ground control are covered in Module

00:22.363 --> 00:25.600
7. Your site's plans always come first.

00:26.724 --> 00:29.374
In the pit, stay on the roads and walkways you're

00:29.374 --> 00:32.637
shown. Berms along ramps and at dump points keep

00:32.637 --> 00:34.774
equipment from going over the edge;

00:34.774 --> 00:37.512
report any berm that's been knocked down or washed

00:37.512 --> 00:40.337
out. Don't park or stand where a backing truck

00:40.337 --> 00:42.812
could reach you, and always make contact with an

00:42.812 --> 00:44.699
operator before you approach.

00:45.822 --> 00:48.110
Spoil banks and stockpiles can give way at the

00:48.110 --> 00:51.722
edge or slide at the toe. Dump short of soft edges,

00:51.722 --> 00:54.847
use the berm, never walk at the toe of a pile,

00:54.847 --> 00:56.559
and never climb a stockpile.

00:59.885 --> 01:02.485
Quarry water is often deep and cold,

01:02.485 --> 01:05.885
with steep sides and soft bottoms. At Allen,

01:05.885 --> 01:08.534
a life jacket is required wherever there's a danger

01:08.534 --> 01:11.334
of falling into water, like working on pumps or

01:11.334 --> 01:14.559
near pond edges. Never walk on ice in a pit.

01:14.559 --> 01:17.272
Know where the ring buoy is. Every one of our sites

01:17.272 --> 01:20.784
has pumps, sumps or ponds, so this applies wherever

01:20.784 --> 01:21.684
you work.

01:25.010 --> 01:27.798
Our sites don't run night shifts, but you can still

01:27.798 --> 01:30.648
work in poor light: early winter mornings and late

01:30.648 --> 01:34.248
afternoons, fog and storms, and inside the plant.

01:34.248 --> 01:37.335
Work areas must be lit well enough to work safely.

01:37.335 --> 01:39.923
Report lights that are out. In low light your depth

01:39.923 --> 01:42.298
perception and side vision are worse,

01:42.298 --> 01:45.785
and operators see less. Wear your reflective hi-vis,

01:45.785 --> 01:49.173
carry a light, slow down, and make contact with

01:49.173 --> 01:52.173
operators before approaching, even more carefully

01:52.173 --> 01:53.360
than in daylight.

01:54.476 --> 01:57.288
Long shifts and early starts bring fatigue.

01:57.288 --> 01:59.189
If you're too tired to work safely,

01:59.189 --> 02:01.389
or you're on medication that affects you,

02:01.389 --> 02:02.814
tell your supervisor.

02:03.926 --> 02:07.089
Recap: stay on roads and walkways and keep berms

02:07.089 --> 02:10.439
intact. Stay off the toe of piles. Life jacket

02:10.439 --> 02:13.651
near water, never on ice. Light up the work,

02:13.651 --> 02:16.014
and make yourself visible in low light.

02:17.144 --> 02:20.306
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

02:20.306 --> 02:21.807
override this video.
